        "1. What impact do missing values have on data analysis?\n",
        "\n",
        "Missing values can reduce the amount of information available and may lead to biased or inaccurate results. They can also affect statistical calculations and Machine Learning models; depending on their amount and cause, missing values can be removed or replaced using methods such as mean, median, mode, or model-based imputation.\n",
        "\n",
        "2. How can we detect and handle outliers in biomedical datasets?\n",
        "\n",
        "Outliers can be detected using box plots, scatter plots, histograms, z-scores, or the interquartile range (IQR). In biomedical data, an outlier should not automatically be deleted because it may represent a real medical condition, researchers should first determine whether it is a measurement error or a valid observation. Incorrect values can be corrected or removed, while valid extreme values may be retained or handled with robust statistical methods.\n",
        "\n",
        "3. What are some common causes of missing or incorrect data in biomedical studies?\n",
        "\n",
        "Common causes include equipment or sensor failures, human entry errors, incomplete questionnaires, patient withdrawal, incorrect measurements, communication problems between devices, and inconsistent data formats, biological variability can also produce values that appear unusual but are actually correct.\n",
        "\n",
        "4. How does normalizing data improve the performance of Machine Learning models?\n",
        "\n",
        "Normalization puts numerical variables on comparable scales. This prevents variables with larger numerical ranges from dominating those with smaller ranges, it can improve the performance and convergence of models, particularly neural networks, k-nearest neighbors, and support vector machines.\n",
        "\n",
        "5. Why is visualizing data an important step before applying Machine Learning models?\n",
        "\n",
        "Visualization helps researchers understand the distribution, relationships, trends, correlations, missing values, and outliers in the data. It can also reveal patterns that may indicate problems with data collection or preprocessing, this information helps determine which preprocessing methods and Machine Learning algorithms are appropriate.\n",
        "\n",
        "6. Why is preprocessing critical when working with medical datasets?\n",
        "\n",
        "Medical datasets often contain missing values, noise, outliers, different measurement scales, duplicated records, and inconsistent formats. Preprocessing improves data quality and makes the dataset suitable for analysis, good preprocessing can produce more reliable and accurate Machine Learning results and reduce the risk of drawing incorrect conclusions.\n",
        "\n",
        "7. What ethical concerns should be considered when handling patient data?\n",
        "\n",
        "Patient data should be handled with privacy, confidentiality, security, and informed consent in mind. Personal identifiers should be protected or removed when possible, and access should be limited to authorized personnel, researchers should also consider potential bias, ensure that data are used only for appropriate purposes, and comply with applicable laws and institutional ethical requirements."
      ],
